# kant over the corpus's shared atoms, written by phil/corpus from readings/kant/logic: not to be edited
logic	s5
atom	cannot_repay	he will not be able to repay the money
atom	promises	he promises stoutly to repay it in a definite time
atom	lent	something will be lent to him
atom	resolves	he resolves to get out of the difficulty by making this promise
atom	maxim_false_promise	the maxim of his action is: when I think myself in want of money, I will borrow money and promise to repay it, although I know that I never can do so
atom	consistent_welfare	this principle of self-love is consistent with my whole future welfare
atom	holds_law_nature	the maxim holds as a universal law of nature
atom	univ_law	it is a universal law that everyone in a difficulty may promise whatever he pleases with the purpose of not keeping the promise
atom	self_contradict	the maxim contradicts itself
atom	promise_exists	the promise itself exists
atom	end_attained	the end one might have in view in the promise is attained
atom	none_believe	no one considers that anything was promised to him, but ridicules all such statements as vain pretences
P1	S2	cannot_repay
P2	S2	¬promises → ¬lent
P3	S4	resolves → maxim_false_promise
P4	S5	◇consistent_welfare
P5	S7	¬◇holds_law_nature
P6	S7	□(univ_law → self_contradict)
P7	S8	univ_law → none_believe
P8	S8	none_believe → ¬◇promise_exists ∧ ¬◇end_attained
P9	S8	univ_law → ¬◇promise_exists ∧ ¬◇end_attained
